<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoki Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoki was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the west of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tottori-prefecture">Tottori Prefecture</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast, including Mount Daisen and the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonago">Yonago</a>. From 1617 it formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tottori">Tottori</a> domain of the Ikeda family together with neighbouring Inaba, and it was merged into Tottori Prefecture after the abolition of the domains in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoki-province.jpg" alt="Hoki Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Hoki.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
